        "original_id": "702d6fc9-5962-57ce-82df-a7ff16708e12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jhené Aiko, Chris Brown, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled, Big Sean\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Projects: Detroit, Sail Out, I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Organizations: Def Jam Recordings\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's I Am Not a Human Being, Rick Ross' Teflon Don, Triple C's Custom Cars & Cycles, DJ Khaled's Kiss The Ring, and Big Sean's Detroit mixtape.\n- Detroit includes American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.\n- Sail Out is the debut EP by American recording artist Jhené Aiko.\n- Sail Out was released on November 12, 2013, through Def Jam Recordings.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
